{"requirements":[{"id":"entry-point","requirement":"Restore an executable, legacy-compatible bin/deliver that accepts one RFC822 message on standard input.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The POSIX-shell entry point was installed executable, passed shell syntax validation, and successfully consumed sample messages from standard input before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e2eeb3a671624e47","cmd-5cdd75f351784617","cmd-b255d0926b1e4f19"]},{"id":"routing","requirement":"Route accounts mail to Maildir/accounts/new, support mail to Maildir/support/new, and all other mail to Maildir/general/new, matching header names case-insensitively.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct tests produced the expected counts in all three destinations. The lowercase support header was routed correctly, and the inspected implementation normalizes header names before comparison.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b76dbc73244545fd","cmd-e2eeb3a671624e47","cmd-5cdd75f351784617","cmd-b255d0926b1e4f19"]},{"id":"integrity-and-uniqueness","requirement":"Preserve every delivered message byte-for-byte and keep repeated-subject deliveries separate.","status":"satisfied","summary":"cmp checks established byte identity for all routes. Two identical accounts submissions created two distinct files, and further deliveries remained separate after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5cdd75f351784617","cmd-b255d0926b1e4f19"]},{"id":"retain-samples","requirement":"Retain the staged sample messages unchanged.","status":"satisfied","summary":"All three sample SHA-256 hashes matched the preparation baseline before testing, after testing, and after restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-5cdd75f351784617","cmd-df56962af4f04041","cmd-b255d0926b1e4f19"]},{"id":"platform-preservation","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with that platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"AlmaLinux 9.6 and kernel 5.14.0-570.12.1.el9_6.x86_64 were unchanged. The solution uses already-present shell utilities and remained functional after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e4f08a16c15741d9","cmd-b255d0926b1e4f19","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.95,"summary":"Changes were narrowly related to implementation, bounded testing, and the mandatory restart. The only unwanted executor-caused residue was /tmp/mail-filter-routing-deliver.before: creating it provided rollback safety, but it remained after successful completion and should have been removed. No failed services, new exposure, or package damage was observed; socket differences were only post-reboot PID changes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e2eeb3a671624e47","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct functional evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete: node1 had a pre-restart boot identity and healthy task state, acknowledged the reboot, returned with a different boot identity corroborated by lifecycle observations, retained existing deliveries, and successfully processed new messages. The sole notable hygiene issue is one retained temporary backup file.","limitations":["Case-insensitive behavior was exercised with canonical-case accounts and lowercase support headers rather than an exhaustive set of header-name case permutations; the captured implementation directly shows normalization with tolower.","Lifecycle snapshots do not inventory the task directory, so file-level final state relies on the executor's direct post-restart checks."]}
